            {
              "id": "6a3b73c8-aad8-3be8-b65e-5f5be5969195",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the memory copy operation. The destination and source may refer to overlapping memory, as indicated by the dataflow analysis. Additionally, there is no explicit check to ensure that the source pointer is not null, which could also lead to undefined behavior. The use of the memory copy function without overlap protection in this context is unsafe and may result in unpredictable program behavior or security issues.\n\n## In Context Remediation 1\nBefore performing the memory copy, add a check to ensure that the source and destination memory regions do not overlap. If overlap is possible, use a safe memory move function that handles overlapping regions correctly. For example:\n\n```cpp\nif ((registers != nullptr) && ((char*)registers + sizeof(_registers) <= (char*)&_registers || (char*)&_registers + sizeof(_registers) <= (char*)registers)) {\n    memcpy(&_registers, registers, sizeof(_registers));\n} else if (registers != nullptr) {\n    memmove(&_registers, registers, sizeof(_registers));\n}\n```\nThis code first checks for null pointers and then determines if the memory regions overlap. If they do, it uses a safe memory move function instead of a direct memory copy.\n\n## In Context Remediation 2\nReplace the direct memory copy with a safe memory move function that is designed to handle overlapping memory regions. For example:\n\n```cpp\nif (registers != nullptr) {\n    memmove(&_registers, registers, sizeof(_registers));\n}\n```\nThis approach ensures that the operation is safe even if the source and destination memory regions overlap.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n___\n"
